event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":98,"item_id":"rs_081718ccfa729843016acae87aaa188190be6e6dc745115805","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating date edit logic**\n\nI'm working on how to handle date edits that are overwritten while preserving the DOM with keyed rows. The simplest approach might rely on reusing the row DOM and updating only the fields that have changed. It’s crucial to ensure that old task forms don’t create problems, so I want to map the mutable saved states into the original task object using Object.assign. Then, I can focus on rendering rows with changes efficiently, updating only if necessary and keeping track of pending drafts."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":99,"item_id":"rs_081718ccfa729843016acae87aaa188190be6e6dc745115805","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating date edit logic**\n\nI'm working on how to handle date edits that are overwritten while preserving the DOM with keyed rows. The simplest approach might rely on reusing the row DOM and updating only the fields that have changed. It’s crucial to ensure that old task forms don’t create problems, so I want to map the mutable saved states into the original task object using Object.assign. Then, I can focus on rendering rows with changes efficiently, updating only if necessary and keeping track of pending drafts."}}

